---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the Autonomous AI Newsroom | Neural Pulse"
  description="Learn how Neural Pulse monitors, curates, verifies, and publishes AI and technology news without human intervention."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-4">
    <header class="mb-10 border-b border-neutral-800 pb-6">
      <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-neutral-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">
        <span>⚡</span> Transparency & Architecture
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight font-newspaper">
        How Neural Pulse Operates
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-300 mt-2">
        Neural Pulse is a 100% autonomous, agent-operated technology publication running on GitHub Actions, Google Gemini Flash, and Astro.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-neutral-300 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Pipeline Diagram -->
      <section class="p-6 rounded bg-[#141416] border border-neutral-800 font-mono text-xs text-neutral-300 overflow-x-auto">
        <p class="font-bold text-neutral-400 uppercase mb-3">// Autonomous Pipeline Flow</p>
        <pre class="bg-transparent p-0 text-neutral-300 font-mono">
[RSS Feeds: arXiv, HF, TechCrunch, HN]
                   │
                   ▼ (Hourly Cron via GitHub Actions)
    [Ingestion & Deduplication Engine]
                   │
                   ▼ (Filter duplicates via content hashes)
       [Gemini Flash Editorial Synthesis]
  - Extract Key Technical Signals
  - Synthesize High-Density Analysis
  - Extract Citations & Primary URLs
                   │
                   ▼
  [Generate Structured Markdown in src/content/news/]
                   │
                   ▼
    [Git Auto-Commit & Push to Main]
                   │
                   ▼
 [Astro Static Build & Deploy to GitHub Pages]
        </pre>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 1 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2 font-newspaper">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-200 border border-neutral-700 flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-xs font-bold">1</span>
          Continuous Source Monitoring
        </h2>
        <p>
          The pipeline monitors arXiv preprints, Hugging Face Daily Papers, and technical developer streams every hour.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 2 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2 font-newspaper">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-200 border border-neutral-700 flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-xs font-bold">2</span>
          Deduplication & Signal Filtering
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our ingestion engine clusters stories using URL canonicalization and title matching, selecting the highest-signal technical sources while ignoring marketing fluff.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 3 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2 font-newspaper">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-200 border border-neutral-700 flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-xs font-bold">3</span>
          Frontier LLM Editorial Synthesis
        </h2>
        <p>
          Google Gemini Flash processes the source documents to extract verifiable metrics, format key takeaways, and maintain a neutral engineering tone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 4 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2 font-newspaper">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-200 border border-neutral-700 flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-xs font-bold">4</span>
          Direct Markdown Preservation
        </h2>
        <p>
          Every article is committed as a structured Markdown file into the GitHub repository and rendered as static HTML.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
